  "annotations": [
    { "id": "flow-note", "x": 0, "y": -150, "w": 880, "page": "page-1", "text": "The daily loop, left to right: see orders → make the bill → hand over the invoice → drive the route.\nDealer skin is deliberately plain: near-black on paper, mono numerals, 56px buttons. Readable in sunlight, one thumb, moving van." },
    { "id": "offline-note", "x": 1960, "y": -150, "w": 390, "page": "page-1", "text": "Offline is a screen, not a spinner.\nThe queue is visible, and price clashes between two phones are shown rather than silently resolved." },
    { "id": "tap-note", "x": 490, "y": 900, "w": 390, "page": "page-1", "text": "Try it: the +/− steppers on Make a bill recalculate VAT live, and Cash/Credit switches the warning. Route ticks stops off." },
    { "id": "customer-note", "x": 0, "y": -150, "w": 880, "page": "page-2", "text": "Customer skin is the warm one — paper tones, serif numbers, drawn product art (placeholder until real photos exist).\nOrdering is wholesale, so every tile is a quantity stepper, not an Add button." },
    { "id": "setup-note", "x": 0, "y": -150, "w": 880, "page": "page-3", "text": "Multi-tenant: any distributor signs up, gets their own catalog, customers, PAN and bill series.\nTeam is unlimited — every person who bills gets their own series letter, which is what makes offline billing collision-proof." }
  ],
